{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781127-ghost-rider-anakim-nemesis","id":781127,"title":"Ghost Rider = Anakim Nemesis?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-06T07:32:50-08:00","id":781127,"title":"Ghost Rider = Anakim Nemesis?","content":"I know he works better as a Sin-Eater, but that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> Nightmares can obviously stand in for the Penance Stare, but how do you include the motorcycle? Magic items aren't very Beastly, and while you can say that the motorcycle is an extension of the Horror, I don't see any way to back that up mechanically.<br /> <br /> His chains could be represented by an Atavism like that Flesh Harpoon Nyrufa homebrewed (I can't find the post for some reason). The rest should be easy enough.<br /> <br /> I'll have to spend more time to come up with his Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-06-2015, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:26:54-08:00","id":781375,"title":"","content":"Eshmaki or Namtaru, with one of the easier to impose Lair Traits, such as Poor Light or Exposed, and a lot of dabbling, as far as Atavisms are concerned. Needs Must, Mimir's Wisdom, Looming Presence, and Nightmares handle the Penance Stare, while Monster From the Deep, Shadowed Soul, Dragon Fire, and Unbreakable handle his physical prowess. The bike would likely be an extension of his Lair; afaik, it's not a specific bike or companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:16:58-08:00","id":781504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781127-ghost-rider-anakim-nemesis#post781127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His chains could be represented by an Atavism like that Flesh Harpoon Nyrufa homebrewed (I can't find the post for some reason). The rest should be easy enough.<br /> <br /> I'll have to spend more time to come up with his Lair Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do link me to that Atavism if you manage to find it. As for what Family he could be, Ghost Rider struck me as either an Eshmaki or an Ugallu. The latter especially when I remember that line of his, &quot;Your soul is stained by the blood of the innocent&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for Lair traits, these ones came to mind.<br /> <br /> Blazing Light &lt;Minor&gt;<br /> Burning &lt;Major&gt;<br /> Darkness &lt;Major&gt;<br /> Extreme Heat &lt;Minor&gt;<br /> Crushing &lt;Major&gt;<br /> Poor Light &lt;Minor&gt;<br /> <br /> I'd also suggest converting the Wound Tilt from this thread (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/763609-hunting-ground-tilts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...g-ground-tilts</a>) as a possible Major Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:36:32-08:00","id":781932,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I can't find it either. Can't even remember the name of the post I put it in.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the motorcycle, he could just drive a normal one in the real world, and drive one made of flaming bones in his lair. Nightmare powers would allow him to ignite his bike, leaving flaming skid marks on the road.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/508934-ideas-for-atavisms\">Found it</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-07-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T14:16:13-08:00","id":790477,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Nyrufa.<br /> <br /> I initially considered Anakim to be his Family because of his incredible strength, and how hellbent (pun intended) he is on punishing evildoers, no matter if they are mortals, supernaturals or gods. You can throw an entire building or a dozen explosives at him and he'll get back up and keep hunting you. There is no way of running from him forever or sweet-talking him into leaving you alone, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rsePyOUvinA\" target=\"_blank\"><b>not even if you are a succubus</b></a>. He's also a larger than life figure who would not be out of place on a heavy metal album cover.<br /> <br /> Namtaru does fit, though he's the kind of repulsive that makes you shit your pants instead of vomit. He isn't fond of niceties and small-talk either.<br /> <br /> I think the Birthright of the Anakim is a bit redundant (destroy a physical obstacle in your way once per scene), since they have Cyclopean Strength and Titanic Blow as two of their Family Atavisms. Being hard to kill is one of the Namtaru's Atavisms (Unbreakable), and their Birthright helps with intimidation IIRC. Ghost Rider might be a Namtaru who happens to have Anakim Atavisms.<br /> <br /> Why Eshmaki, though? He doesn't seem like a very shadowy or subtle vigilante to me, though he's certainly cunning.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Deionscribe, why the Crushing Lair Trait? Is that meant to be his motorcycle running people over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-21-2015, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T16:38:10-08:00","id":790556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781127-ghost-rider-anakim-nemesis?p=790477#post790477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Birthright of the Anakim is a bit redundant (destroy a physical obstacle in your way once per scene), since they have Cyclopean Strength and Titanic Blow as two of their Family Atavisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring Durability and being able to lift huge things don't translate to &quot;in a single turn, you can break through any physical obstacle regardless of your other stats.&quot; An Anakim can bypass a steel door or a wall of force even with Strength 1, Lair 1, and Brawl 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T17:52:11-08:00","id":790586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/781127-ghost-rider-anakim-nemesis?p=790556#post790556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring Durability and being able to lift huge things don't translate to &quot;in a single turn, you can break through any physical obstacle regardless of your other stats.&quot; An Anakim can bypass a steel door or a wall of force even with Strength 1, Lair 1, and Brawl 0.</div> </div> </div> </div> You got me there, as usual. I should have remembered that not every Anakim is a combat powerhouse, just like not every Ventrue is an expert politician. You can totally have an Anakim who is the brains of the group and whose only Family Atavism is Mimir's Wisdom. The feeling of Powerlessness need not be caused by curb-stomping. It can also be caused when not even your best rhetoric and realpolitik can bring someone down from their position.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}